    "top_frame": "The offense didn't find a pulse until it was too late.",
    "what_this_means": "Mahle gave them nothing to work with. Five strikeouts in 5.1 innings. Clean command, no damage. And the Giants couldn't generate anything meaningful until the game had already moved on without them. Schmitt got his two hits, Ramos got one, but six hits and a single run against a pitcher who carried a 5.00 ERA before tonight feels less like they competed and more like they showed up. The pattern has shifted into something more predictable and harder to fix: they're not just inconsistent anymore. They're quiet until the moment passes. Eight games below .500 now. The division gap widened. This is what happens when pitching keeps you in games but the bats arrive too late to matter. The math is real. One run doesn't win baseball games.",
